 17592186424016 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186424019 #edb/ref 1069 "q-136920" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186424019 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186424019 #edb/ref 1071 "$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}2{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+{x}_{3}=0 \\\\ 4{x}_{1}+2{x}_{2}+2{x}_{3}=1\\end{aligned}\\,\\,[\\begin{aligned}20 & 10 & a \\\\ 10 & 5 & 5 \\\\ c & 5 & 5\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}b \\\\ 2 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the system of linear equations and its corresponding normal equation shown above. What is the value of $a+b+c?$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186424019 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "4cb13173-852b-58a2-8c1f-3d6511a05fac" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186424019 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we write our system in matrix form as $Ax=b,$ where \n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 4 & 2 & 2\\end{aligned}],\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}],\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nThe normal equation corresponding to $Ax=b$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{T}\\,Ax & ={A}^{T}b \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}2 & 4 \\\\ 1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 4 & 2 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 4 \\\\ 1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}20 & 10 & 10 \\\\ 10 & 5 & 5 \\\\ 10 & 5 & 5\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\na+b+c=10+4+10=24.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
